-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADDITIONAL TELECOMMUNICATIONS, EMERGENCY CALLING & PRIVACY NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. NO EMERGENCY CALLING GUARANTEE (112 / 911 / 999 / E911):
   AiPBX is open-source software and is NOT a certified public emergency call
   routing service. Power outages, internet/network disruptions, SIP trunk
   failures, or dialplan misconfigurations may prevent emergency calls from
   completing or from transmitting accurate location information. Always
   maintain an independent landline or mobile path for emergency services.

2. TELECOM BILLING, SECURITY & TOLL FRAUD RESPONSIBILITY:
   Connecting a PBX to PSTN / SIP trunks carries inherent financial risk. The
   person or entity deploying AiPBX is solely responsible for securing server
   access, enforcing strong credentials, restricting firewall and outbound
   routing rules, and monitoring call traffic. The authors and contributors
   shall not be liable for any telecom charges, toll fraud, or unauthorized
   call costs incurred through your SIP providers or carriers.

3. CALL RECORDING, FAX & AI PROCESSING COMPLIANCE (GDPR / KVKK / PRIVACY LAWS):
   Features such as call recording, voicemail transcription, signaling capture,
   and cloud or local AI integrations process potentially sensitive personal
   and communications data. Enabling and operating these features in compliance
   with applicable telecommunications, wiretapping, caller-consent, and data
   protection laws (including GDPR, KVKK, and local regulations) is the sole
   responsibility of the system operator.

